tests/i86corpus/ -- .CMD files tests/i86test.c reads.  Test input, nothing else.

PIP.CMD, ED.CMD, GENCMD.CMD and SUBMIT.CMD are Digital Research's own CP/M-86
1.0 programs, unmodified, from the cpm86pc drop of the Unofficial CP/M Web
Site.  Licensed by the 9 July 2022 grant from Bryan Sparks (President, DRDOS,
Inc.) at <http://cpm.z80.de/license.html>, which carries no distribution
restriction.

They are 8086 code.  Nothing on this machine executes them and nothing stages
them onto a disk image: our utilities are native Z8000 programs -- src/cmd/
pip.c and src/cmd/stat.c are DRI's sources rebuilt as .Z8K, and they beat
anything a shim can interpret.  These four are here because a loader needs
real headers to be tested against, and because a PIP copy is a known-answer
test for the day the CP/M-86 shim can make a BDOS call.
